      (ADDRESS = (PROTOCOL = TCP)(HOST = odc3oradev7.dc.gov)(PORT = 1762))

    )

    (CONNECT_DATA =

      (SERVICE_NAME = archbprd)

    )

  )

We are experiencing performance issue for below schema. Can you please check for any long running queries and fine tune them?

URL = "jdbc:oracle:thin:@(DESCRIPTION=(ADDRESS=(PROTOCOL=TCP)(HOST= passprddb.dc.gov)(PORT=1762))(LOAD_BALANCE=OFF)(CONNECT_DATA=(SERVER=DEDICATED)(SERVICE_NAME=passprd)))";
User = INVOICEPROD;

Like ticket UR0326381, when calling an Oracle Spatial package, an error is generated on GEOPRD2 but not on GEOPRD1. Before, we would get a Java error message on GEOPRD2. Now, after the patching, the session is immediately terminated with ORA-03113: end-of-file on communication channel.
Here's the test code:
declare
  l_geom_wkt            clob;
  l_geom_from           sdo_geometry;
begin
  l_geom_wkt := 'POINT (10 10)';
  dbms_output.put_line('Instance: ' || upper (SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV','INSTANCE_NAME')));
  l_geom_from := sdo_util.from_wktgeometry(l_geom_wkt);
end;
/

